  "verbalization": "Nigrolineaxanthone F appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to SNU1, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first pathway links Nigrolineaxanthone F to G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, which is then targeted by LHQIJBMDNUYRAM-BBIVZNJYSA-N, a protein that in turn targets SNU1. The second and third pathways connect Nigrolineaxanthone F to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by Teyin and Phorone, both of which also target SNU1. These findings indicate that Nigrolineaxanthone F may act through distinct molecular pathways to influence SNU1, potentially through different mechanisms such as enzyme inhibition or protein interaction. The shared targeting of SNU1 across multiple pathways suggests a possible role for Nigrolineaxanthone F in modulating cellular processes that involve SNU1, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
